% ============================================================================
% fable-moral.query.adj — worked recall over the fable-moral library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is this fable's
% moral?" (direct) or "which fable has this moral?" (reverse) — it states
% no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks
% binding queries.
% ============================================================================

import "fable-moral.adj"

? fable_moral(tortoise_and_the_hare, $Moral)   % expect "Slow but steady wins the race." (direct)
? fable_moral($F, $Moral)                       % expect all three fables and their morals (reverse over everything)
? fable_moral(the_fox_and_the_crow, $Moral)     % expect abstain -- its closing line is character dialogue, not a narrator-stated moral
